<section class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 space-y-12">
  <article class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-black dark:text-white mb-6">How to Calculate Your Final Grade</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        <p>
          Calculating your required final exam score involves understanding <strong>weighted averages</strong>. 
          Most college and high school courses divide your grade into categories like Homework (20%), 
          Midterms (40%), and the Final Exam (20-40%).
        </p>
        <p>
          The formula our calculator uses is:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-4 rounded-xl font-mono text-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-800 text-blue-700">
          Required = (Target - (Current × (1 - Weight))) / Weight
        </div>
        <p>
          Where <em>Weight</em> is the percentage your final exam is worth, expressed as a decimal.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/40 border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white mb-4">Step-by-Step Manual Guide</h3>
        <ul class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">
          <li>Multiply your current grade by (100% - final exam weight).</li>
          <li>Subtract that result from your target overall grade.</li>
          <li>Divide the remainder by the final exam weight.</li>
          <li>The result is the score you need on the final!</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-black dark:text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <details class="group bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/50 border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl transition-all duration-300">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer list-none">
          <span class="text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">What is a weighted grade?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="p-4 pt-0 text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A weighted grade means different assignments are worth more than others. For example, a final exam worth 30% of your grade has the same impact as 30 homework assignments worth 1% each.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/50 border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl transition-all duration-300">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer list-none">
          <span class="text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">How do "Drop Lowest" calculations work?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="p-4 pt-0 text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Our calculator allows you to input specific points to drop from your total. This effectively removes those points from the denominator of your grade calculation, raising your current percentage.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/50 border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl transition-all duration-300">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 cursor-pointer list-none">
          <span class="text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">What if the calculator says it's "out of reach"?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="p-4 pt-0 text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          It means that even with a perfect 100% on the final exam, the math just doesn't add up to your target grade. But hey, you are more than a single grade. Take a deep breath, reset your target to something achievable, and use our study tools to finish the semester strong.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
